From 97424a370da7ae8c8f603267b0d1391cd71e90a9 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Aditya Suresh <adityasuresh22@gmail.com>
Date: Fri, 16 Oct 2026 17:08:54 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] [Bugfix][Model Loader] Evict loaded shards when checkpoint
 exceeds RAM

When the safetensors checkpoint is larger than 90% of available RAM (the
rule that already turns off auto-prefetch), evict each shard from the page
cache with posix_fadvise(DONTNEED) once the caller has released its last
tensor. Page cache counts toward a container's memory usage, and a
checkpoint that size cannot stay fully cached for the next load anyway.

Only the default mmap path (None and "lazy") on Linux. Checkpoints that
fit are untouched, and so are eager, torchao and prefetch loads. The last
shard is still referenced when the iterator ends, so it is left to the
kernel.

Signed-off-by: Aditya Suresh <adityasuresh22@gmail.com>
---
 tests/model_executor/test_weight_utils.py     | 46 ++++++++++++++++++
 vllm/config/load.py                           |  4 +-
 .../model_loader/weight_utils.py              | 47 ++++++++++++++++---
 3 files changed, 89 insertions(+), 8 deletions(-)

